From: Beryl 7 reproducible build <beryl7-build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: beryl7: enable the SuperSpeed USB PHY

The MT7987 base device tree disables its USB 3 port and connects only the
USB 2 PHY.  Override both settings for the Beryl 7, whose external USB port
is wired for SuperSpeed.  This matches the vendor board device tree and the
upstream Banana Pi R4 Lite configuration using the same MT7987 controller.

---
 .../dts/mt7987a-glinet-gl-mt3600be.dts        | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-glinet-gl-mt3600be.dts b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-glinet-gl-mt3600be.dts
index 784e134fff..3e840b351c 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-glinet-gl-mt3600be.dts
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/dts/mt7987a-glinet-gl-mt3600be.dts
@@ -277,6 +277,9 @@
 };
 
 &ssusb {
+	mediatek,u3p-dis-msk = <0>;
+	phys = <&tphyu2port0 PHY_TYPE_USB2>,
+	       <&tphyu3port0 PHY_TYPE_USB3>;
 	vbus-supply = <&usb_vbus>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
2.47.3
